} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 4+0\\cdot (-4)}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{6\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5})≈{63}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269137 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269138 13194139533962 true] [17592186269137 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269139 13194139533962 true] [17592186269137 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269140 13194139533962 true] [17592186269137 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269141 13194139533962 true] [17592186269137 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269142 13194139533962 true] [17592186269137 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533962 true] [17592186269137 1041 "selection" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269137 1104 #edb/ref 17592186269141 13194139533962 true] [17592186269137 1110 #uuid "e4556650-d240-5520-9d69-8f8ef1163437" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269138 1034 "{90}^{∘}" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269138 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533962 true] [17592186269138 1111 #uuid "853ea703-1d96-539c-87e3-e34d3d095438" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269139 1034 "{27}^{∘}" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533962 true] [17592186269139 1111 #uuid "d0f223ca-0fea-5bae-8cdd-b11ad4571b15" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269140 1034 "{88}^{∘}" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533962 true] [17592186269140 1111 #uuid "12fb3ba3-823c-5cfc-b083-6ce78c505fcd" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269141 1034 "{63}^{∘}" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533962 true] [17592186269141 1111 #uuid "e05e7500-7274-5b9b-90bd-0b84dc643510" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269142 1034 "{57}^{∘}" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269142 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533962 true] [17592186269142 1111 #uuid "9a09a8bd-4160-5cba-b8e6-8131c8959abe" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269143 1017 #edb/ref 17592186269144 13194139533962 true] [17592186269143 1089 "q-77159" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269143 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533962 true] [17592186269143 1100 "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(2,4,1),$ $Q(3,4,2)$ and $R(3,3,1).$" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269143 1113 #uuid "09283c16-ce85-51a9-9e26-ee1e56005470" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269143 1145 "Note that the position vectors of the points $P,$ $Q$ and $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨2,4,1⟩,\\,q=⟨3,4,2⟩,\\,r=⟨3,3,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨3,4,2⟩-⟨2,4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨3,3,1⟩-⟨2,4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})={60}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139533962 true] [17592186269144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269145 13194139533962 true] [17592186269144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269146 13194139533962 true] [17592186269144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269147 13194139533962 true] [17592186269144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269148 13194139533962 true] [17592186269144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186269149 13194139533962 true] [17592186269144 1040